{"step_index":5509,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T17:04:56Z","thinking":"At a high threshold, a significant number of items were filtered, while a smaller subset remains for review. Initial review of the remaining items reveals valid distinctions in product strength and potential OCR errors. These discrepancies warrant further investigation to determine accurate categorization.\n\n\nReview reveals valid distinctions: differing strengths and insulin types within the remaining candidates. Examining the filtered items confirms the filtering effectively removed dissimilar drug names. Increasing the candidate pool from three to six presents an opportunity to refine filtering, potentially reducing ambiguous cases for LLM analysis.\n\n\nThe expanded candidate pool increases the likelihood of finding a direct match, reducing the \"unresolved\" category. A safety net mechanism now guides ambiguous matches towards pharmacist review, specifically when a strong brand match exists but concentration, form, or dosage conflicts are present. This safeguards against misclassifying similar drugs as complete mismatches while also accounting for OCR errors. This refinement aims to improve match accuracy and reduce overall manual review needs.\n\n\nThe initial calculation was off; verifying the current match counts against the total shortage items reveals a logical distribution across matched, review, and not-found categories. Reviewing the match function reveals the candidate count and safety net logic. Examination of the code determines how the system attempts to auto-match and classifies items for review based on a defined safety check.\n\n\nThe auto-match logic must be revised, specifically removing the broad similarity thresholds to enforce strict safety checks based on brand, form, drops, syrup, and strength. The candidate pool for ambiguous cases is increased to improve LLM analysis, sending the top five candidates for each shortage. A safety net mechanism is in place that redirects potentially similar matches to pharmacist review to avoid misclassification.\n\n\nA series of logical checks are now in place to detect critical mismatches, specifically focusing on syrup formulations, solid dosage strengths, and drug forms. Differences in these key aspects trigger pharmacist review. Furthermore, if a shortage is in drop form but the candidate is not, that's flagged.\n\n\nBrand similarity is calculated using multiple fuzzy matching techniques and a brand family check to assess potential matches. Logic now incorporates considerations for brand, form, co-formulation, syrup, and drops. A mismatch in any of these critical features triggers a review requirement, even if brand similarity is high.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\fast_match\\coordinator.py","EndLine":190,"StartLine":55,"toolAction":"View is_safe_auto_match in coordinator.py","toolSummary":"Check is_safe_auto_match lines"}}]}
{"step_index":5510,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T17:05:07Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-23T20:05:07+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-23T20:05:07+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/src/fast_match/coordinator.py`\nTotal Lines: 568\nTotal Bytes: 34296\nShowing lines 55 to 190\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n55:    - As long as the trade brand name, dosage form, and strength match:\r\n56:      - Different ampoule counts (e.g. 3 ampoules vs 6 ampoules vs 1 ampoule vs 25 ampoules / 6امبول vs 3امبول) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n57:      - Different pack counts (e.g. 20 tablets vs 30 tablets vs 60 tablets vs 5 tablets) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n58:      - Different strip counts (e.g. 2 strips vs 3 strips vs 5 strips) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n59:      - Retail unit vs wholesale carton/bundle (e.g. 20 tablets vs باكت 32, باكت 200, 32ب) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n60:      - Strips vs total tablets (e.g. 3 strips vs 12 tablets) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n61:      - Missing pack count or quantity on either side -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n62:      - Manufacturer suffixes (/فاركو, /جلاكسو), commercial indicators (\"س ج\", \"سعر جديد\", \"سعر قديم\") do not change the product.\r\n63:      - NEVER mark tablet count, ampoule count, pack count, or wholesale carton differences as \"review\" or \"no_match\"!\r\n64: \r\n65: 5. THE \"REVIEW\" (يحتاج مراجعة) SAFETY NET:\r\n66:    - \"review\" is the essential SAFETY NET for the pharmacist to manually inspect borderline cases.\r\n67:    - If there is any doubt, borderline OCR scanning, minor ambiguity, or 25%–70% plausibility:\r\n68:      ALWAYS ROUTE TO \"review\" instead of rejecting to \"no_match\"!\r\n69:    - A potential match in \"review\" allows the pharmacist to verify availability in the warehouse, whereas dropping an item into \"no_match\" causes the pharmacy to lose an available medicine.\r\n70:    - Examples for \"review\":\r\n71:      - Conflicting bottle/tube volume of liquids/semi-solids when BOTH sides explicitly specify different numbers (e.g. requested 15ml drops vs candidate writes 5ml drops).\r\n72:      - Borderline OCR where brand letters are slightly ambiguous but plausibly the same drug.\r\n73:      - When you are uncertain between \"review\" and \"no_match\": ALWAYS CHOOSE \"review\".\r\n74: \r\n75: SCHEMA:\r\n76: Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:\r\n77: {\r\n78:   \"results\": [\r\n79:     {\r\n80:       \"case_id\": \"string\",\r\n81:       \"status\": \"match\" | \"review\",\r\n82:       \"item_id\": \"string (the matching candidate ID)\",\r\n83:       \"reason\": \"string (Arabic explanation when review, otherwise empty string)\"\r\n84:     }\r\n85:   ]\r\n86: }\r\n87: \r\n88: CRITICAL RULES FOR RESPONSE:\r\n89: - ONLY include cases that are \"match\" or \"review\".\r\n90: - DO NOT return cases that are \"no_match\" (any omitted case_id is automatically considered no_match).\r\n91: - DO NOT return markdown blocks (no ```json). Return ONLY the raw JSON starting with { and ending with }.\r\n92: \"\"\"\r\n93: \r\n94: def norm_num(s: str) -> str:\r\n95:     s = str(s)\r\n96:     for e, w in zip('٠١٢٣٤٥٦٧٨٩', '0123456789'):\r\n97:         s = s.replace(e, w)\r\n98:     return s\r\n99: \r\n100: def get_strength_pattern(text: str) -> str | None:\r\n101:     text = norm_num(text.lower())\r\n102:     m = re.search(r'(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*(?:مجم|مج|جم|جرام|gm|mg|mcg|مكجم)', text)\r\n103:     if m:\r\n104:         return m.group(1)\r\n105:     if 'ربع' in text or '25.' in text:\r\n106:         return '0.25'\r\n107:     if 'نص' in text or 'نصف' in text or '.5' in text or '0.5' in text:\r\n108:         return '0.5'\r\n109:     return None\r\n110: \r\n111: def has_co(text: str) -> bool:\r\n112:     t = text.lower()\r\n113:     return bool(re.search(r'(?:^|[^\\w])(كو|بلس|بلاس|كومب|co|plus|comp)(?:[^\\w]|$)|كواقراص|كوأقراص|بلساقراص|بلسكبسول', t))\r\n114: \r\n115: def are_forms_compatible(form1: str | None, form2: str | None) -> bool:\r\n116:     if not form1 or not form2:\r\n117:         return True\r\n118:     if form1 == form2:\r\n119:         return True\r\n120:     compat = {\r\n121:         ('tablet', 'capsule'), ('capsule', 'tablet'),\r\n122:         ('cream', 'ointment'), ('ointment', 'cream'),\r\n123:         ('cream', 'gel'), ('gel', 'cream'),\r\n124:         ('injection', 'ampoule'), ('ampoule', 'injection'),\r\n125:     }\r\n126:     return (form1, form2) in compat\r\n127: \r\n128: BRAND_FAMILIES = {'بيتادين', 'هيرو', 'انسولين', 'ليمتلس', 'سيتال', 'لبن'}\r\n129: \r\n130: def is_safe_auto_match(req: str, cand: str) -> tuple[bool, str]:\r\n131:     brand_r = extract_brand_tokens(req)\r\n132:     brand_c = extract_brand_tokens(cand)\r\n133:     if not brand_r or not brand_c:\r\n134:         return False, \"no_brand\"\r\n135:         \r\n136:     words_r = brand_r.split()\r\n137:     words_c = brand_c.split()\r\n138:     \r\n139:     first_r = words_r[0]\r\n140:     first_c = words_c[0]\r\n141:     if first_r in BRAND_FAMILIES or first_c in BRAND_FAMILIES:\r\n142:         if fuzz.ratio(brand_r, brand_c) < 85:\r\n143:             return False, \"brand_family_ambiguity\"\r\n144:             \r\n145:     b_sim = fuzz.ratio(brand_r, brand_c)\r\n146:     if words_r and words_c and (words_r[0] == words_c[0] or fuzz.ratio(words_r[0], words_c[0]) >= 85):\r\n147:         if len(words_r) == 1 and len(words_c) == 1:\r\n148:             b_sim = max(b_sim, 90)\r\n149:             \r\n150:     if b_sim < 85:\r\n151:         return False, \"low_brand_sim\"\r\n152:         \r\n153:     form_r = extract_form_group(req)\